      "name": "DetectGlideBoards",
      "signature": "bool DetectGlideBoards(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Detects the number of Glide-compatible graphics boards in the system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Call grGet(GR_NUM_BOARDS=0x0F, 4, &g_dwNumGlideBoards) to query board count\n  2. Log \"Detecting boards which support Glide...\" via QueueLogMessage\n  3. Log \"\\t%d boards found\" with the count via QueueLogMessage\n  4. Return TRUE (1) if board count > 0, FALSE (0) otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  None - this function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  BOOL - TRUE (1) if at least one Glide-compatible board detected\n         FALSE (0) if no Glide boards are available\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns FALSE if grGet returns 0 boards\n  - The board count is stored in global g_dwNumGlideBoards (0x6f885434)\n  - Function is called via vtable g_vtblGlideRenderer at 0x6f881030\n\nNotes:\n  - GR_NUM_BOARDS (0x0F) is a Glide API constant for querying board count\n  - Function body extends from 0x6f871870 to 0x6f8718ab\n  - Uses SETG instruction for boolean conversion (count > 0)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
