      "name": "InitializeGamePools",
      "signature": "undefined InitializeGamePools(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes all game object pools with cleanup mode (param=0).\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Call FUN_6f873ff0(&g_pItemPool, 0) - Initialize/cleanup item pool\n  2. Call FUN_6f876c00(&g_pMonsterPool, 0) - Initialize/cleanup monster pool\n  3. Call FUN_6f877130(&g_pObjectPool, 0) - Initialize/cleanup object pool\n  4. Call FUN_6f877130(&g_pMissilePool, 0) - Initialize/cleanup missile pool\n  5. Call FUN_6f877130(&g_pUnitPool, 0) - Initialize/cleanup unit pool\n\n  Parameters:\n  (none)\n\n  Returns:\n  void - Modifies global pool structures in place\n\n  Special Cases:\n  All pools are cleared with cleanup mode (second param=0), completely \n  zeroing out their contents. No memory allocation, only deallocation.",
