      "name": "PlayIntroVideo",
      "signature": "undefined PlayIntroVideo(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Plays a Bink video file with optional looping if game not aborting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if g_dwGameAbort flag is 0 (game not terminating)\n  2. If game is aborting, return immediately\n  3. Clear graphics buffer to black (0, 0, 0)\n  4. Swap graphics buffer to display cleared frame\n  5. Set g_bVideoPlaying flag to 1 (indicate video playback active)\n  6. Call PlayBinkVideo with file path and loop count\n  7. Clear g_bVideoPlaying flag to 0 (video playback complete)\n\nParameters:\n  szBinkFilePath  - Pointer to null-terminated Bink video file path\n  nLoopCount      - Number of times to loop the video (1+ for looping)\n\nReturns:\n  void (no explicit return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If g_dwGameAbort is non-zero at entry, function returns immediately\n  without playing the video. This allows graceful termination when the\n  game needs to shut down during video playback initialization.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:5fc30c789debbc776c3f29902f1def963cd4b47eadfb53b0a90095717bf4cf6a",
