      "name": "ConvertScreenBufferTo24Bit",
      "signature": "undefined4 ConvertScreenBufferTo24Bit(byte * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Converts 565 RGB screen buffer to 24-bit RGB format using Glide API\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Lock Glide frame buffer with grLfbLock(0, 1, 0xFF, 0, 0, ...)\n  2. For each scanline (height = g_dwScreenHeight):\n     a. For each pixel in scanline (width = g_dwScreenWidth):\n        i. Extract R5 from bits 15-11: (pixel >> 8) & 0xF8\n        ii. Extract G6 from bits 10-5: (pixel >> 5) << 2\n        iii. Extract B5 from bits 4-0: pixel << 3\n        iv. Write 3 bytes as RGB to output buffer\n     b. Advance input pointer by scanline stride\n  3. Unlock frame buffer with grLfbUnlock(0, 1)\n  4. Return success (1) or failure (0)\n\nParameters:\n  pRgbBuffer  Pointer to output buffer for 24-bit RGB pixel data\n\nReturns:\n  1 on success (frame buffer locked and converted)\n  0 on failure (grLfbLock failed)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.03",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b2a261452534050f235ca97b19c128c5599a83e2b058850b4f92754a075744f5",
