      "name": "SetColorCombineState",
      "signature": "undefined SetColorCombineState(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Sets graphics color combine state based on input mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load current graphics state from g_dwGraphicsState0\n  2. If state is 0 or nState differs from current state, process:\n     - If nState == 1 (0x1): Call grColorCombine(3, 1, 0, 1, 0)\n     - If nState == 2 (0x2): Call grColorCombine(1, 0, 1, 2, 0)\n  3. Update g_dwGraphicsState0 to new state\n  4. Return\n\nParameters:\n  nState (ECX)  State ID: 1 for mode A, 2 for mode B\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If current state matches nState, skips grColorCombine call (optimization)\n  - State 0 is initial/invalid, always processes state change\n  - Invalid states (not 1 or 2) are silently ignored",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:3288dd7e995d860cb2bb23cd82d242917675c64edaddbfde4fb2ac2ae1efbf04",
