      "name": "SetTextureFilterMode",
      "signature": "undefined SetTextureFilterMode(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Configures texture filtering mode for all active texture memory units.\nManages graphics state transitions and calls grTexFilterMode with appropriate\nparameters based on the filter mode value. Supports up to 2 TMUs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current graphics state (g_dwGraphicsState2) to ECX\n2. If state is 0 or matches new mode, return early (no state change)\n3. Otherwise, decode mode parameter into filter settings:\n   - Mode 1: Set both TMUs to (filter=0, param=0)\n   - Mode 2: Set both TMUs to (filter=1, param=1)\n4. Only configure TMU1 if TMU count (g_dwTmuCount) > 1\n5. Store new mode in g_dwGraphicsState2\n\nParameters:\n  ECX (nFilterMode): Filter mode value (1 = mode1, 2 = mode2)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if current state matches requested mode\n- Configuration is idempotent; repeated calls with same mode are safe\n- Requires g_dwTmuCount > 0 to be valid (at least TMU0)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:56daad7971252e3f41e5a8fc1693ab595a9e709745c6e6c7a8a83bf6dc39b591",
