      "name": "InitializeGlideTextures",
      "signature": "int InitializeGlideTextures(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes Glide texture system with mipmap download tables and state structures\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Normalize nHeight: if high bit set (0x80), OR with 0x80 and increment; else use as-is\n  2. Normalize dwWidth: if high bit set, OR with dwWidth and increment; else use as-is\n  3. Calculate mipmap levels: (dwWidth * 3) << 5 = dwTexDataSize\n  4. Allocate texture data buffer (0x80 bytes header + dwTexDataSize data)\n  5. Initialize texture pointer at g_pTextureData (0x6f881810)\n  6. For each texture (256 entries at 0x6f8865e8):\n     a. Copy 0x20 DWORDs (32 bytes) from g_aTexTableBase (0x6f8867e4) to EDI\n     b. Call grTexDownloadMipMap to register texture with graphics subsystem\n     c. Increment pointer by 4 bytes, add row offset to dimension counter\n  7. Release allocation buffer via ReleasePoolAllocation\n  8. Initialize global state fields with default values and constants\n\nParameters:\n  dwWidth (ECX): texture width in pixels\n  nHeight (EDX): texture height in pixels\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: Always returns 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles texture dimensions with sign extension (0x80 bit)\n  - Processes 256 texture entries in sequential iteration\n  - Initializes 19 global state variables with fixed-point values (0x3f800000=1.0, 0x43800000=256.0)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.02",
