      "name": "RenderFormattedTextString",
      "signature": "undefined RenderFormattedTextString(int param_1, int param_2, LPCSTR param_3, va_list param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders a printf-style formatted text string to the Glide framebuffer using a bitmap font.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format the input string using wvsprintfA with the provided va_list arguments\n2. Initialize graphics state: set color combine, alpha blend, texture filter, and texture combine modes\n3. Iterate through each character in the formatted string:\n   a. If X position exceeds 640 (0x280), set character width to 0 (clipping)\n   b. If X position is negative, use character's width from width table (scrolling text)\n   c. For printable ASCII chars (0x20-0x7F):\n      - Configure vertex quad coordinates for 8-pixel wide character cell\n      - Set texture source from font texture table (character code - 0x20)\n      - Draw character quad via grDrawVertexArrayContiguous\n      - Get character width from spacing table\n   d. For non-printable characters, use default width\n4. Advance cursor X position by character width\n5. On newline (0x0A): reset X to initial value, advance Y by 12 pixels (line height)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT ECX (in_ECX): nXPos - Initial X coordinate for text rendering\n- IMPLICIT EDX (in_EDX): nYPos - Initial Y coordinate for text rendering\n- lpszFormat: Printf-style format string (ANSI)\n- pArgList: Pointer to va_list argument list for format string\n\nReturns:\n- void - Renders directly to graphics hardware, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- X > 640: Characters clipped (width=0), prevents overflow\n- X < 0: Characters still processed for width calculation (scrolling support)\n- Newline char (0x0A): Line feed, advances Y by 12 pixels, resets X\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x280 (640): Maximum X coordinate before clipping\n- 0x20 (32): ASCII space, first printable character\n- 0x7F (127): DEL, last character in font table\n- 0x08: Character cell width in pixels\n- 0x0C (12): Line height in pixels for newline\n- 0x10 (16): Y offset for bottom of character cell\n- 0x1C (28): Stride for vertex data structure\n\nStructure Layout (Vertex Quad at g_adwData_6f8865f0):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n0x5e    0x04  flTopLeftX      float   Top-left X coordinate\n0x5f    0x04  flTopLeftY      float   Top-left Y coordinate\n0x65    0x04  flTopLeftX2     float   Copy of top-left X\n0x66    0x04  flBottomY       float   Bottom Y (Y + 16)\n0x6c    0x04  flTopRightX     float   Top-right X (X + 8)\n0x6d    0x04  flBottomY2      float   Copy of bottom Y\n0x73    0x04  flBotRightX     float   Bottom-right X (X + 8)\n0x74    0x04  flBotRightY     float   Copy of top-left Y",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
