      "name": "InitializeGraphicsBuffers",
      "signature": "undefined InitializeGraphicsBuffers(undefined4 * param_1, undefined4 * param_2, undefined4 param_3, undefined4 param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes graphics rendering buffers from source data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Store configuration parameters in g_dwGraphicsConfig1 and g_dwGraphicsConfig2\n  2. Copy 0x400 (1024) DWORDs from pSrcBuffer1 to g_aGraphicsBuffer1 (4096 bytes)\n  3. Copy 0x1200 (4608) DWORDs from pSrcBuffer2 to dynamically allocated buffer via g_pGraphicsBufferPtrs\n  4. Call DrawColorPatternTestGrid() to render test grid with initialized buffers\n\nParameters:\n  pSrcBuffer1 (ECX)   - Pointer to first source buffer (palette/color data)\n  pSrcBuffer2 (EDX)   - Pointer to second source buffer (rendering data)\n  dwConfig1 (stack)   - Graphics configuration parameter 1\n  dwConfig2 (stack)   - Graphics configuration parameter 2\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, performs initialization side effects\n\nNotes:\n  - Called during graphics subsystem initialization\n  - Buffers are used by DrawColorPatternTestGrid() for test grid rendering\n  - Configuration values may control color palette or rendering mode",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c48d22f7de29ed56769ce5ca6370a89a0cba463f432a5da34926f22f37296b6a",
