      "name": "DrawRect",
      "signature": "undefined DrawRect(int param_1, float param_2, int param_3, int param_4, uint param_5, byte param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Draws a filled rectangle, line, or single point using Glide3 graphics API.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate all coordinates are within screen bounds (0 to max dimension)\n  2. Convert input color to internal format via GetColorValue()\n  3. Set color combine state to mode 2\n  4. Configure alpha blend mode: 1 for full alpha (0xFF), 4 for partial alpha\n  5. If partial alpha, combine color with alpha value: (color & 0xFFFFFF00) | alpha\n  6. Disable chromakey mode, set constant color value\n  7. If X1==Y1 and X2==Y2 (decompiler artifact from coordinate comparison):\n     - Build GrVertex with coords and Z=1.0\n     - Draw single point via grDrawPoint()\n  8. Otherwise build two GrVertex structures and draw line via grDrawLine()\n  9. Re-enable chromakey mode before return\n\nParameters:\n  nX1 (ECX): Starting X coordinate, must be >= 0 and < screen width\n  nX2 (EDX): Ending X coordinate, must be >= 0 and < screen height\n  nY1 (Stack+0x4): Starting Y coordinate, must be >= 0 and < screen width\n  nY2 (Stack+0x8): Ending Y coordinate, must be >= 0 and < screen height\n  dwColor (Stack+0xC): ARGB color value (masked to extract color index)\n  bAlpha (Stack+0x10): Alpha value (0x00-0xFF); 0xFF means full opacity\n\nReturns:\n  void - Renders directly to framebuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Point: When both X coords equal AND both Y coords equal, draws single point\n  - Line: Uses grDrawLine with two GrVertex structures\n  - Out of bounds: Returns without drawing if coordinates exceed screen dimensions\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x3f800000: Float 1.0 (Z coordinate for vertex)\n  - 0xFF: Full alpha/opacity value\n  - 1: Alpha blend mode for full alpha\n  - 4: Alpha blend mode for partial alpha\n  - 2: Color combine state mode\n\nStructure Layout (GrVertex):\n  Offset  Size  Field  Type   Description\n  0x00    4     x      float  X coordinate\n  0x04    4     y      float  Y coordinate\n  0x08    4     z      float  Z coordinate (always 1.0)\n  0x0C    4     oow    float  1/w for perspective (always 0)\n  0x10    4     tmu    float  TMU data (always 0)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.03",
      "method": "NOP",
