      "name": "DrawDiamondRect",
      "signature": "undefined DrawDiamondRect(int * param_1, undefined4 param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Draws a diamond/X pattern rectangle with gradient coloring\n  \nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate rectangle bounds (left < right, top < bottom)\n  2. Calculate width and height from bounds\n  3. Calculate center points (midpoint coordinates)\n  4. Verify bounds are within screen dimensions (0x00 to g_dwScreenWidth/Height)\n  5. Draw 4 rectangles forming X pattern:\n     - Top-right triangle: center to right-bottom (dwColor)\n     - Bottom-right triangle: center to left-bottom (dwBorderColor)\n     - Bottom-left triangle: center to left-top (dwBorderColor)\n     - Top-left triangle: center to right-top (dwBorderColor)\n\nParameters:\n  pRect (ECX): pointer to rectangle bounds [left, top, right, bottom]\n  dwColor (stack): fill color for main triangle (0xAARRGGBB)\n\nReturns:\n  none\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If width or height is 0, function returns without drawing\n  - Bounds must pass validation (left < right && top < bottom)\n  - All coordinates must be within screen bounds",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.03",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:6278a85d360a6b5f2c83d3b914d7751934f887bab2f6478b93aa794ce10cfa04",
