      "name": "DrawRectangleWithMargin",
      "signature": "undefined DrawRectangleWithMargin(int * param_1, char param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Draws a rectangle with a computed margin offset from base coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate margin parameter (must be non-zero)\n  2. Compute margin offset: (char - 1) as unsigned value\n  3. Create RECT structure with margin applied to all sides\n  4. Call DrawRectangle with adjusted coordinates\n\nParameters:\n  pCoords       : Pointer to integer array [x, y] for rectangle center\n  byMargin      : Margin size as character code (1 = 0 pixel, 2 = 1 pixel, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n  void          : No explicit return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If byMargin == 0 (null char), function skips rectangle drawing entirely\n  - Margin offset is computed as (byMargin - 1), allowing values 1-255\n  - Rectangle bounds: x\u00b1offset, y\u00b1offset",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
