      "name": "RenderTileData",
      "signature": "undefined RenderTileData(byte * param_1, byte * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders tile projection data with color/vertex information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. ProcessTileProjectBuffer validates tile data (returns nonzero if valid)\n  2. Check color byte at [pTileData+0] for 0xFF to set alpha blend mode\n  3. Set color combine state and texture filter mode via SetColorCombineState/SetTextureFilterMode\n  4. Decompress primary tile color using lookup table:\n     bytes [0-3] -> 2-byte index into pColorLookup -> store dwPrimaryColor\n  5. Load float X,Y coords from [pTileData+4] and [pTileData+8]\n  6. Decompress secondary color from bytes [0x3c-0x3f], store with floats\n  7. Decompress tertiary color from bytes [0x1a4-0x1a7], store with floats\n  8. Call grDrawVertexArray to render primary tile with current graphics state\n  9. If vertex data missing: loop 36 vertices, each with 0x0c byte stride\n  10. For each vertex: decompress color, store to buffer, render batch via grDrawVertexArray\n\nParameters:\n  pTileData (ECX): Tile structure at 0x1b0+ bytes containing:\n    [0-3]: Packed color bytes (index+decompression)\n    [4], [8]: X,Y float coordinates for primary tile\n    [0x3c-0x3f], [0x40], [0x44]: Secondary color and coords\n    [0x1a4-0x1a7], [0x1a8], [0x1ac]: Tertiary color and coords\n    [0x168-0x16b], [0x16c], [0x170]: Additional color vertex data\n  pColorLookup (EDX): 256-color palette lookup table for decompression\n\nReturns:\n  void - Renders to graphics buffer, modifies global rendering state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If color byte == 0xFF: uses alpha blend mode 1 (fully opaque)\n  Otherwise: uses alpha blend mode 4 (standard blending)\n  Handles missing vertex data via fallback loop path",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:47a67e43c8df4208e4824d91b63990896aebdd0edad027e4a09ef9f988aa8c0c",
