      "name": "InitializeCache",
      "signature": "int InitializeCache(uint * param_1, int param_2, uint param_3, uint param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes a cache structure for storing and managing item references.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate number of cache items: (dwMaxAddress - dwMinAddress) / dwItemSize\n  2. Allocate memory pool for cache items (0x14 bytes per item)\n  3. Initialize pCache structure fields (offsets 0, 4, 7, 8, 12, 16, 20)\n  4. Build cache item linked list with forward/backward pointers\n  5. Set initial cache pointers (free list, head, tail)\n  6. If UMA not supported, scan for address boundary violations:\n     - Item addresses must not cross 0x200000 boundary\n     - Skip items that would violate boundary constraints\n     - Adjust item count and tail pointer if needed\n\nParameters:\n  pCache (ECX) - Pointer to cache structure to initialize\n  dwMinAddress (EDX) - Minimum address for cache item data\n  dwMaxAddress (ESP+4) - Maximum address for cache item data\n  dwItemSize (ESP+8) - Size of each data item in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  EAX - Total size allocated (dwNumItems * dwItemSize)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
