      "name": "CalculateGraphicsMemoryLayout",
      "signature": "int CalculateGraphicsMemoryLayout(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Calculates aligned graphics memory layout for sprite buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Compute adjusted size as (nMemorySize - 1) to normalize range\n  2. Determine high 16-bit alignment: if bit 15 set, add 0x10000 for carry\n  3. Combine with base alignment: OR adjusted size with dwBaseAlignment\n  4. If overlap detected (non-zero), increment to next aligned boundary\n  5. Store aligned base offset and compute total needed size\n  6. Initialize sprite buffer pointers to source buffers\n  7. Return double of aligned memory (stride calculation)\n\nParameters:\n  ECX: dwBaseAlignment - memory alignment mask (0x8000 = 32KB boundary)\n  EDX: nMemorySize - requested memory size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: dwAlignedMemory * 2 (stride for next allocation block)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Handles bit 15 alignment detection for 16-bit boundary wrap-around\n  Computes allocation offset accounting for dual-buffer configuration",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d844f23667d21c9c771ad6c53f1ff464bac07528a3bf1279246c699a611d20df",
