      "name": "ReleaseSpriteRenderingBuffers",
      "signature": "undefined ReleaseSpriteRenderingBuffers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Releases all sprite rendering pipeline buffers\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if g_pSpriteBuffer0 is allocated (non-NULL)\n     - If allocated, call ReleasePoolAllocation to free (line 0x56/86)\n     - Set g_pSpriteBuffer0 to NULL\n  2. Check if g_pSpriteBuffer1 is allocated (non-NULL)\n     - If allocated, call ReleasePoolAllocation to free (line 0x5b/91)\n     - Set g_pSpriteBuffer1 to NULL\n  3. Check if g_pSpriteBuffer2 is allocated (non-NULL)\n     - If allocated, call ReleasePoolAllocation to free (line 0x60/96)\n     - Set g_pSpriteBuffer2 to NULL\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Safe to call even if buffers not allocated (NULL check before release)\n  - Counterpart to InitializeSpriteRenderingBuffers which allocates these buffers\n  - Each buffer is 0x8000 (32KB) when allocated\n  - Uses FogMemPool release mechanism via ReleasePoolAllocation\n  - Source file: D2Gfx/sprite.cpp (based on debug path)",
