      "name": "ClearResourceData",
      "signature": "undefined ClearResourceData(int * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Clears resource data at specified coordinates from game resource table\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize loop counter to 5 (0x5)\n  2. Validate both coordinates are >= 1 (param_1[0] - 1 >= 0 AND param_1[1] - 1 >= 0)\n  3. Calculate resource table base: g_aGameResourceTable + (X - 1) * 0x20 (32 bytes per row)\n  4. Calculate target field offset: base + 0x8 + (Y - 1) * 0x1c (28 bytes per field)\n  5. Clear target field to 0x0 (4 bytes)\n  6. Move to next coordinate pair in input buffer\n  7. Repeat steps 2-6 until 5 coordinate pairs processed\n\nParameters:\n  ECX pCoords - Pointer to array of coordinate pairs (10 ints total: X1,Y1,X2,Y2,...,X5,Y5)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\npfnCallback parameter of SetCelfileCallback\n",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
