      "name": "CalculateTextureDimensions",
      "signature": "undefined CalculateTextureDimensions(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Calculates texture buffer dimensions and mipmap scaling factors.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate width bucket from param_1[4]: maps to power-of-2 (8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256)\n  2. Calculate height bucket from param_1[8]: maps to power-of-2 (8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256)\n  3. Determine max dimension and compute mipmap level (log2 of max)\n  4. Calculate aspect ratio correction:\n     - If width < height: right-shift height, set correction from g_aScaleDownFactorsNegative\n     - If height < width: right-shift width, set correction from g_aScaleDownFactorsPositive\n     - If equal: no correction (0x0)\n  5. Set pixel format based on background color:\n     - Color 0: initialize as 1.0, compute X/Y texture coords, fetch max Y from g_fMaxTextureCoordY\n     - Other: initialize as 1.0 with zero scaling\n\nParameters:\n  pTexture (ECX): Pointer to texture structure\n    [+0x4] = dWidth: Input width value (0-255+)\n    [+0x8] = dHeight: Input height value (0-255+)\n    [+0x14] = Output width bucket\n    [+0x18] = Output height bucket\n    [+0x1c] = Pixel count (width * height)\n    [+0x20] = Unknown flag (set to 0x0)\n    [+0x24] = X texture coordinate or 1.0\n    [+0x28] = Y texture coordinate or 0.0\n    [+0x2c] = Alpha value (1.0)\n    [+0x30] = Mipmap level (3-8)\n    [+0x34] = Aspect ratio correction factor\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Width/height < 8: buckets to 0x8\n  - Width/height = 8-16: buckets to 0x10\n  - Dimension buckets: 0x20, 0x40, 0x80, 0x100\n  - Loop limitation: max 3 iterations for scaling adjustment",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0e59997ed2a164f0ac30d061b5394ee68f31e93eba68b752c1eb4f825772bbbd",
