      "name": "LoadAndDrawCelFile",
      "signature": "undefined4 LoadAndDrawCelFile(int * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Loads and renders a CEL graphics frame to screen with alpha blending.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load or retrieve CEL frame data at index 0, frame 1\n  2. Validate CEL file pointer, retrieving default if null\n  3. Extract CEL file table index, height, mode, and Y coordinate from data\n  4. Validate rendering bounds against screen dimensions (0x6f881bc4, 0x6f881bcc)\n  5. Calculate texture dimensions based on frame data\n  6. Load CEL texture into graphics buffer\n  7. Configure alpha blending mode (0-2: 0x40/0x80/0xc0, 3-4: blend 2/3, 5-7: blend 1)\n  8. Render texture vertices to screen with color key and palette index\n\nParameters:\n  pCelData: Pointer to CEL file data structure\n  nXPos: Horizontal screen position (X coordinate)\n  dwColorKey: Color key for transparency (palette index or RGBA value)\n  nBlendMode: Blend mode 0-7 controlling alpha transparency\n  nPaletteIndex: Palette index for texture color mapping\n\nReturns:\n  0 if bounds validation failed or texture load failed\n  1 if rendering completed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Blend modes 5 and 7 use alpha blend 1 (standard transparency)\n  - Blend modes 3 and 4 use alpha blends 2 and 3 (darker/lighter)\n  - Default modes 0-2 use dithering with constant color (0x40-0xc0 alpha)\n  - CelFileInfo pointer dereferenced from first DWORD of pCelData",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:408a99d9c3bab13f80cb300c6ca76b2821327ccc8bdc54d3239d73e9feb7a216",
