      "name": "RemoveItemByIndex",
      "signature": "undefined RemoveItemByIndex(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Removes an item from a doubly-linked list at specified index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load item count from pListHead+0x8\n  2. If count is 0, return (empty list)\n  3. Call FUN_6f876ed0(pListHead, nIndex) to find item at index\n  4. If item not found, decrement count and return\n  5. Clear item's linked list pointer at offset 0x8\n  6. If list head pointer (pListHead+0x14) is NULL (first item):\n     a. Set head pointer to new item\n     b. Set tail pointer to new item\n  7. Otherwise, insert item at end:\n     a. Link previous tail's next pointer (offset 0xc) to new item\n     b. Set new item's prev pointer (offset 0x10) to old tail\n     c. Update tail pointer to new item\n  8. Decrement item count\n\nParameters:\n  pListHead (ECX): Pointer to doubly-linked list head structure\n  nIndex (EDX): Index of item to remove (0-based)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset|Size|Field        |Type      |Description\n  0x8   |4   |nItemCount   |dword     |Number of items in list\n  0x14  |4   |pHead        |void*     |Pointer to first item\n  0x18  |4   |pTail        |void*     |Pointer to last item\n\nLinkedList Node Layout:\n  Offset|Size|Field        |Type      |Description\n  0x8   |4   |pListHead    |void*     |Back reference to list head\n  0xc   |4   |pNext        |void*     |Next node pointer\n  0x10  |4   |pPrev        |void*     |Previous node pointer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
