      "name": "ReleaseTextureTableAllocation",
      "signature": "void ReleaseTextureTableAllocation(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Releases the texture table memory pool allocation and clears the global reference.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if g_pTexTableBase is allocated (non-zero)\n  2. If allocated, call ReleasePoolAllocation() to free the memory\n  3. Clear g_pTexTableBase to NULL (0) to prevent dangling pointer\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  None (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_pTexTableBase is already NULL, function exits immediately\n  - Must be called before final cleanup in CloseGlideWindow()\n  - Part of texture resource cleanup sequence",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
