      "name": "SetColorFromPalette",
      "signature": "undefined SetColorFromPalette(int param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Sets a color value at destination from a 256-color palette table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Extract color index low byte and scale by 0x100 (256) for palette offset\n  2. Load 3 color component indices from DAT_6f886f4c (separated by bytes)\n  3. Look up each component value in palette starting at g_pColorPalette\n  4. Combine RGB components into 32-bit DWORD with alpha 0xFF\n\nParameters:\n  pDest [ECX]: Pointer to destination 32-bit DWORD at offset +0x8\n  dwColorIndex [EDX]: Color palette index (0-255), passed as DWORD\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Extracts 3 bytes from DAT_6f886f4c at bytes 0x00, 0x08, 0x10\n  - Result stored as ABGR format (alpha=0xFF in high byte)\n  - Palette lookup uses g_pColorPalette as base address",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:2203c21f5fec57dd56a478b68622ae47c2fd9a7117d644e32711de0b10a0da03",
