      "name": "DecodeColorPaletteIndex",
      "signature": "undefined DecodeColorPaletteIndex(int param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Decodes a palette-indexed color and stores the RGB result at destination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Extract palette index from bits 0-7 (dwPaletteIndex & 0xFF)\n  2. Shift left by 8 to get offset into g_pColorPalette (index * 0x100)\n  3. Add to palette base address: dwPaletteBase = g_pColorPalette + offset\n  4. Extract R from bits 8-15: *(byte*)(dwPaletteBase + (dwPaletteIndex >> 8 & 0xFF))\n  5. Extract G from bits 16-23: *(byte*)(dwPaletteBase + (dwPaletteIndex >> 16 & 0xFF))\n  6. Extract B from bits 24-31: *(byte*)(dwPaletteBase + (dwPaletteIndex >> 24))\n  7. Pack into 32-bit ARGB (MSB=R, followed by G, B; LSB unused)\n  8. Store result at pDest+0x8 as DWORD\n\nParameters:\n  ECX (pDest): Pointer to structure where color will be stored at offset +0x8\n  EDX (dwPaletteIndex): Packed color index (PaletteID.RGB format)\n\nReturns:\n  (none - void function, result stored at [pDest+0x8])\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Palette base g_pColorPalette must be initialized before calling\n  - No bounds checking on palette indices\n  - Alpha channel (bits 24-31) set to 0xFF (opaque)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:8c4109f0327b9d635bce15c65ee0833628a49709cb1518d2ed02561baf82b19b",
