      "name": "InitializeGammaAndColorTables",
      "signature": "undefined InitializeGammaAndColorTables(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes gamma correction and color shift lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize gamma correction control values (0x6f887100-0x6f887168)\n     with FLT_1.0 (0x3f800000) and FLT_256.0 (0x43800000) constants\n  2. Populate g_aGammaLookupTable (0x6f886f68) with nested loops:\n     - Outer loop: iVar5 (0 to 3) = vertical iteration\n     - Inner loop: iVar4 (0 to 3) = horizontal iteration\n     - Each entry stores: [-1]=1.0, [0]=(iVar4<<7), [1]=(iVar5<<6)\n     - Stride between elements: 0x1c (28) bytes\n  3. If g_dwColorTableInitialized not set, process g_aColorShiftTable:\n     - Loop through table, left-shift each 32-bit entry by 0x10 (16 bits)\n     - Table range: 0x6f881d68 to 0x6f882038\n     - Element stride: 0xc (12) bytes\n  4. Set g_dwColorTableInitialized = 1 to prevent re-initialization\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  None (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - g_dwColorTableInitialized guard prevents redundant color table shifts\n  - Uses floating-point operations on integer data (FILD/FSTP pattern)\n  - Performs in-place 16-bit left-shift on color table entries",
