      "comment": "Convert IEEE 754 double precision (64-bit) to extended precision (80-bit) floating-point format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent (11 bits) and sign bit from double precision format at offset +6\n2. Extract mantissa components from double precision low and high words\n3. Handle special cases: zero values (both parts zero) set output to zero and return\n4. Handle infinity/NaN: if exponent is 0x7FF (2047), set extended exponent to 0x7FFF (32767)\n5. Handle denormalized numbers: if exponent is 0, set bias to 0x3C01 (15361) and clear hidden bit\n6. Normal numbers: convert exponent bias from double (1023) to extended (16383) by adding 0x3C00\n7. Construct extended precision mantissa by combining double parts with proper bit alignment\n8. Normalize mantissa by left-shifting until MSB is set, adjusting exponent accordingly\n9. Store final extended precision format: mantissa in pExtended[0-1], exponent+sign in pExtended[2]\n\nParameters:\npExtended - Pointer to output extended precision float (12 bytes: mantissa[8], exponent[2], padding[2])\npDouble - Pointer to input double precision float (8 bytes: low[4], high[4])\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result stored in pExtended output buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\nZero Input: Both pDouble[0] and pDouble[1] mantissa bits zero - outputs zero extended precision\nInfinity: Double exponent 0x7FF becomes extended exponent 0x7FFF  \nNaN: Double exponent 0x7FF with non-zero mantissa preserved as extended NaN\nDenormalized: Double exponent 0x000 handled with special bias and normalization\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7FF0 - Double precision exponent mask (11 bits shifted left 4)\n0x7FF - Maximum double precision exponent (infinity/NaN marker)\n0x7FFF - Maximum extended precision exponent (infinity/NaN marker)  \n0x3C00 - Exponent bias conversion offset (16383 - 1023 = 15360)\n0x3C01 - Denormalized number bias for extended precision (15361)\n0x80000000 - Extended precision hidden bit mask\n0x8000 - Sign bit mask for extended precision format\n0xFFFFF - Double precision mantissa mask (20 bits)\n0x15 - Bit shift count (21) for mantissa alignment\n0xB - Bit shift count (11) for mantissa reconstruction\n\nIEEE 754 Format Layout:\nDouble Precision (64-bit): [Sign:1][Exponent:11][Mantissa:52]\nExtended Precision (80-bit): [Sign:1][Exponent:15][Hidden:1][Mantissa:63]\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking - assumes valid double precision input\nInvalid inputs may produce undefined extended precision results",
