      "name": "AllocateMemoryWithRetry",
      "signature": "void * AllocateMemoryWithRetry(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates zeroed memory with automatic retry on failure via callback handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total allocation size (dwElementCount * dwElementSize)\n2. Align size to 16-byte boundary (add 15, mask with 0xFFFFFFF0)\n3. If size <= g_dwMemoryBlockThreshold (1016 bytes):\n   a. Acquire critical section 9\n   b. Try AllocateMemoryDescriptorBlock for small allocations\n   c. Release critical section\n   d. If successful, zero memory with memset and return\n4. Fall back to HeapAlloc with HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag (0x8)\n5. On allocation failure, invoke callback handler if g_dwNewHandlerFlag set\n6. Retry loop continues while handler returns non-zero\n\nParameters:\n  dwElementCount - Number of elements to allocate\n  dwElementSize  - Size of each element in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Pointer to zeroed memory block on success\n  NULL  - On allocation failure after handler exhaustion\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xFFFFFFE1 - Maximum valid size check (~4GB - 31 bytes)\n  0x0F       - Alignment mask addend (15 bytes)\n  0xFFFFFFF0 - 16-byte alignment mask\n  0x08       - HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag for HeapAlloc\n  9          - Critical section index for memory block allocator\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero-size requests are promoted to 1 byte minimum\n  - Sizes >= 0xFFFFFFE1 skip allocation entirely (overflow protection)\n  - Small allocations (<= 1016 bytes) use fast block allocator\n  - Block allocator failure falls through to heap allocation",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
