      "name": "ParseLocaleString",
      "signature": "uint * ParseLocaleString(uint * param_1, uint * param_2, undefined4 * param_3, undefined4 * param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Processes and validates codec parameters, updating global configuration state.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Check if szInputParam is NULL; return NULL if so\n  2. Special case: if szInputParam is \"C\\0\", set output to 0x43, clear parameter buffers, return\n  3. Compare szInputParam against g_szCurrentCodecParam and g_szPreviousCodecParam\n  4. If no match, parse szInputParam via FUN_00407def into stack buffer\n  5. Validate parsed result via FUN_0040947a; return NULL on failure\n  6. Copy word from g_dwCodecValue to g_dwCodecOutput\n  7. Process globals via FUN_00407ebb\n  8. If szInputParam is empty string, use g_szCurrentCodecParam; copy to g_szPreviousCodecParam\n  9. Copy 6 bytes from g_aCodecConfig to pdwParam3\n  10. Copy 4 bytes from g_dwCodecOutput to pdwParam4\n  11. Copy g_szCurrentCodecParam to szOutputBuffer; return pointer\n\n  Parameters:\n  szInputParam - input codec parameter string (NULL or terminated string)\n  szOutputBuffer - output codec parameter string buffer\n  pdwParam3 - optional output buffer for 6-byte config word array\n  pdwParam4 - optional output buffer for 4-byte DWORD value\n\n  Returns:\n  szOutputBuffer on successful processing; g_szCurrentCodecParam if parameter unchanged;\n  NULL if szInputParam is NULL or validation fails",
