      "name": "GetCachedLocaleInfo",
      "signature": "int GetCachedLocaleInfo(uint param_1, LCTYPE param_2, char * param_3, int param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves locale information from cached table, falling back to GetLocaleInfoA.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Perform binary search on g_aLocaleEntries array (27 entries, 0x1a bounds)\n  2. Array sorted by LCID (dwLCID field at offset 0x00)\n  3. If LCID found, select field based on dwLCType:\n     - LOCALE_SLANGUAGE (0x01): szLanguageCode (offset 0x04)\n     - LOCALE_SABBREVLANGNAME (0x03): szShortLangCode (offset 0x10)\n     - LOCALE_SABBREVCTRYNAME (0x07): szAbbrevLangCode (offset 0x18)\n     - LOCALE_IDEFAULTCODEPAGE (0x0b): szCodePage (offset 0x1c)\n     - LOCALE_SENGLANGUAGE (0x1001): pszCountryName ptr (offset 0x0c)\n     - LOCALE_SENGCOUNTRY (0x1002): pszNativeLangName ptr (offset 0x14)\n     - LOCALE_IDEFAULTANSICODEPAGE (0x1004): szAnsiCodePage (offset 0x24)\n  4. Copy string to buffer with null-termination (max nBufferSize-1 chars)\n  5. If not found or unsupported LCTYPE, call GetLocaleInfoA\n\nParameters:\n  dwLocaleId   - Windows locale identifier (LCID)\n  dwLCType     - Type of locale information to retrieve\n  pszBuffer    - Output buffer for locale string\n  nBufferSize  - Size of output buffer in characters\n\nReturns:\n  1 on success (found in cache)\n  GetLocaleInfoA result on cache miss or unsupported type\n\nStructure Layout (LocaleEntry, 0x2c bytes):\n  Offset | Size | Field             | Type     | Description\n  -------|------|-------------------|----------|---------------------------\n  0x00   | 4    | dwLCID            | uint     | Windows locale ID\n  0x04   | 8    | szLanguageCode    | char[8]  | Language code string\n  0x0c   | 4    | pszCountryName    | char*    | Ptr to country name\n  0x10   | 4    | szShortLangCode   | char[4]  | Short language code\n  0x14   | 4    | pszNativeLangName | char*    | Ptr to native lang name\n  0x18   | 4    | szAbbrevLangCode  | char[4]  | Abbreviated language code\n  0x1c   | 8    | szCodePage        | char[8]  | Default code page\n  0x24   | 8    | szAnsiCodePage    | char[8]  | ANSI code page",
