      "name": "ParseHexStringToInt",
      "signature": "int ParseHexStringToInt(char * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses a null-terminated hexadecimal string and converts it to an integer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize result accumulator to 0\n  2. For each character in string until null terminator:\n     a. If lowercase 'a'-'f' (0x61-0x66): subtract 0x27 (39) to normalize\n     b. If uppercase 'A'-'F' (0x41-0x46): subtract 7 to normalize\n     c. Digits '0'-'9' remain unchanged (ASCII 0x30-0x39)\n  3. Apply formula: result = (result - 3) * 16 + normalized_char\n     - The -3 offset compensates for ASCII '0' base (0x30 = 48 = 3*16)\n  4. Return accumulated integer value\n\nParameters:\n  szHexString - Pointer to null-terminated ASCII hex string (e.g., \"1A2B\")\n\nReturns:\n  int - Parsed integer value from hex string\n  Note: No validation - invalid chars produce undefined results\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty string (\"\") returns 0\n  - Accepts mixed case (e.g., \"aB1c\")\n  - No \"0x\" prefix handling - pass raw hex digits only",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:f0a11635fdf2d320a2e515a84b2db710ef2aec95164517e24f645aaa677d6852",
