      "name": "CopyStringToBuffer",
      "signature": "undefined CopyStringToBuffer(char * param_1, int * param_2, int * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Copies characters from a null-terminated source string to a destination buffer.\nProvides bounded copy functionality for date/time formatting string operations.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Load remaining byte count from *pnRemaining into local cache\n    2. Check if remaining count is 0; exit immediately if no space\n    3. Load source character at current position\n    4. Check if source character is null terminator; exit if end of string\n    5. Copy source character to current destination position (*ppszDest)\n    6. Increment destination pointer through ppszDest\n    7. Decrement remaining count through pnRemaining\n    8. Advance source pointer to next character\n    9. Loop back to step 2 while remaining > 0\n\n  Parameters:\n    szSource      - Pointer to null-terminated source string to copy from\n    ppszDest      - Pointer to destination buffer pointer (updated after each char)\n    pnRemaining   - Pointer to remaining byte count (decremented after each char)\n\n  Returns:\n    void - Updates destination pointer and remaining count in-place via pointers\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - If *pnRemaining is 0 on entry, returns immediately (no copy)\n    - If szSource points to empty string, returns immediately (no copy)\n    - Does NOT append null terminator (caller must handle termination)\n    - Terminates when buffer exhausted OR end of source string reached",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:296d793167cd1bafc8d1ef52b2c7a02d0b9913b0e946d3ad7809ae7dcd8670dc",
