      "name": "ShutdownGlideRenderer",
      "signature": "undefined4 ShutdownGlideRenderer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Cleanup and shutdown the Glide graphics renderer and system resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if Glide graphics subsystem is initialized (g_dwGlideInitialized != 0)\n     - Perform pre-shutdown house keeping via FUN_6f874740()\n     - Clean up initialization state via FUN_6f872220()\n     - Log status message: \"Shutting down Glide...\"\n     - Call Glide API shutdown function grGlideShutdown()\n     - Log status message: \"Glide shut down\"\n     - Free tile cache buffer resources via FreeTileCacheBuffers()\n     - Perform additional cleanup via FUN_6f874410()\n     - Perform final cleanup via FUN_6f877450()\n     - Mark Glide as uninitialized by setting g_dwGlideInitialized = 0\n  2. Check if critical section exists (g_pCriticalSection != 0)\n     - Delete the critical section synchronization object\n     - Release pool memory allocation\n     - Mark critical section as null by setting g_pCriticalSection = 0\n  3. Return success code (1)\n\nParameters:\n  (none - global state only)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Idempotent: safe to call multiple times, handles partial initialization states\n  - No error handling: does not return error codes\n  - Handles Glide and critical section independently",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
