      "name": "GetGameAbort",
      "signature": "uint GetGameAbort(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Checks if game abort is requested and reinitializes Glide graphics if not.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global abort flag (g_bGameAbort at 0x6f885454)\n2. If aborting, return 0 immediately\n3. Save current Glide context pointer\n4. Close existing Glide window (CloseGlideWindow)\n5. Swap and clear Glide buffers (grBufferSwap, grBufferClear)\n6. Select Glide context 0 (grSstSelect)\n7. Reinitialize Glide window (InitializeGlideWindowInternal)\n8. If initialization fails, return 0\n9. Enable Glide rendering (grGlideInit with 0,0,0)\n10. Query gamma table capabilities via grGet:\n    - GR_GAMMA_TABLE_ENTRIES (0x5) -> nGammaEntryCount\n    - GR_BITS_GAMMA_TABLE (0x2a) -> nBitsPerEntry\n11. If gamma entries > 0:\n    a. Allocate gamma table memory (SMemAlloc)\n    b. Calculate max entry value: (1 << nBitsPerEntry) - 1\n    c. Generate gamma correction table (GenerateGammaTable)\n    d. Load gamma table to hardware (grLoadGammaTable)\n    e. Free temporary memory (SMemFree)\n12. If no gamma support, set uniform gamma (guGammaCorrectionRGB with 1.0f)\n13. Return 1 for success\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses global state\n\nReturns:\nuint - 1 if graphics reinitialized successfully, 0 if game abort requested or init failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x5 = GR_GAMMA_TABLE_ENTRIES (Glide grGet parameter)\n0x2a = GR_BITS_GAMMA_TABLE (Glide grGet parameter)\n0x3f800000 = 1.0f (IEEE 754 single precision)\n0x34f, 0x35a = Source line numbers for SMemAlloc/SMemFree\n\nRelated Globals:\ng_bGameAbort (0x6f885454) - Game abort flag\ng_pGlideContext (0x6f885214) - Current Glide SST context pointer\ng_pGammaConfig (0x6f885348) - Gamma configuration pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
