      "name": "ApplyGammaCorrection",
      "signature": "void ApplyGammaCorrection(int nGamma)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Applies gamma correction to the graphics subsystem using either hardware gamma tables or direct RGB scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check global gamma level (g_nGammaLevel) to determine correction path\n  2. If gamma disabled (level <= 0):\n     a. Scale input gamma value by float multiplier from global data\n     b. Apply direct RGB correction via guGammaCorrectionRGB()\n  3. If gamma enabled (level > 0):\n     a. Query graphics device for gamma table support (grGet GR_GAMMA_SUPPORT=5)\n     b. Query number of supported gamma table entries (grGet GR_GAMMA_TABLE_ENTRIES=0x2a)\n     c. Allocate temporary table: nEntries * 4 bytes (DWORD per entry)\n     d. Generate gamma lookup table via GenerateGammaTable()\n     e. Load table into hardware via grLoadGammaTable()\n     f. Free temporary allocation\n\nParameters:\n  nGamma (ECX, int): Gamma correction value to apply, typically in range 0-256.\n                     Higher values increase brightness/contrast.\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Hardware state is modified directly.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If grGet fails (returns 0), function exits silently without applying correction\n  - When gamma disabled, uses simpler float-scaled RGB path\n  - Memory allocated via SMemAlloc with source file tracking for debugging\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x5  : GR_GAMMA_SUPPORT - Glide constant for gamma capability query\n  - 0x2a : GR_GAMMA_TABLE_ENTRIES - Glide constant for table size query\n  - 0x34f: Source line number for allocation tracking (847 decimal)\n  - 0x35a: Source line number for free tracking (858 decimal)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:a56f45caf5a793f8523d0b23f98c1eadef7430902e23b8a809979f8d2fb94f55",
