      "name": "DrawFilledRectangle",
      "signature": "undefined DrawFilledRectangle(uint param_1, uint param_2, uint param_3, uint param_4, uint param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Draws a filled rectangle on the screen using Glide graphics API with coordinate clamping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Clamp dwX1 to valid range [0, g_dwScreenWidth] using conditional masking\n  2. Clamp dwX2 to valid range [0, g_dwScreenWidth]\n  3. Early exit if dwX1 == dwX2 (zero width - degenerate rectangle)\n  4. Clamp dwY1 to valid range [0, g_dwScreenHeight]\n  5. Clamp dwY2 to valid range [0, g_dwScreenHeight]\n  6. Early exit if dwY1 == dwY2 (zero height - degenerate rectangle)\n  7. Assert dwY2 > dwY1 via FogAssert; call ReportError(-1) on failure\n  8. Configure Glide render state: SetColorCombineState(2), SetAlphaBlendMode(4)\n  9. Disable chromakey mode for solid fill rendering\n  10. Build 4-vertex triangle strip on stack (each GrVertex = 28 bytes)\n  11. Extract palette color index from low byte of dwY2 parameter\n  12. Set constant color via grConstantColorValue with alpha from dwColor parameter\n  13. Draw quad as triangle strip: grDrawVertexArrayContiguous(GR_TRIANGLE_STRIP, 4, vertices, 0x1c)\n  14. Re-enable chromakey mode and return\n\nParameters:\n  dwX1 (ECX) - Left edge X coordinate, clamped to [0, screen_width]\n  dwY1 (EDX) - Top edge Y coordinate, clamped to [0, screen_height]\n  dwX2 (Stack+0x4) - Right edge X coordinate, clamped to [0, screen_width]\n  dwY2 (Stack+0x8) - Bottom edge Y coordinate; must be > dwY1 after clamping\n\nReturns:\n  void - Renders directly to Glide framebuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Negative coordinates converted to 0 via (x < 1 ? 0 : x) masking\n  - Coordinates beyond screen bounds clipped to screen dimensions\n  - Zero-width rectangles (X1 == X2) silently skipped\n  - Zero-height rectangles (Y1 == Y2) silently skipped\n  - Height validation failure (Y2 <= Y1) triggers assertion at line 0x61\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3f800000 = 1.0f (IEEE 754) - Used for OOW (1/w) homogeneous coordinate\n  0x1c = 28 bytes - GrVertex structure stride\n  0x5 = GR_TRIANGLE_STRIP primitive type\n  0x4 = 4 vertices for quad rendering\n\nStructure Layout (Stack Vertex Array):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Type    Description\n  0x00    4     flVertex0_X  float   Top-left X (dwX1 clamped)\n  0x04    4     flVertex0_Y  float   Top-left Y (dwY1 clamped)\n  0x08    4     flVertex0_OOW float  1.0f homogeneous W\n  0x0C    4     flVertex0_R  float   Red component (1.0f)\n  0x10    4     flVertex0_G  float   Green component (0.0f)\n  0x14    4     flVertex0_B  float   Blue component (0.0f)\n  0x1C    28    vertex1      GrVertex Top-right vertex\n  0x38    28    vertex2      GrVertex Bottom-left vertex\n  0x54    28    vertex3      GrVertex Bottom-right vertex\n\nGlide API Calls:\n  SetColorCombineState(2) - Configure texture/color combine mode\n  SetAlphaBlendMode(4) - Set alpha blending function\n  grChromakeyMode(0/1) - Disable/enable chromakey transparency\n  grConstantColorValue() - Set fill color from palette\n  grDrawVertexArrayContiguous() - Render triangle strip primitive",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:5cc2d6f90dfff943cd2b4892dd08dbe38069ea71db4fbb824542e488977f0b6a",
