      "name": "RenderCelFrameWithSetup",
      "signature": "undefined RenderCelFrameWithSetup(int * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders a CEL animation frame with full graphics state setup.\n\nConfigures alpha blending and dithering modes before loading and rendering\na CEL frame. Validates the CEL file handle and asserts if null. Uses frame\nindex 1 for loading and applies texture rendering with vertex positioning.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set alpha blend mode to 4 (specific blend configuration)\n2. Disable dithering (grDitherMode(0))\n3. Set constant color value to 0x40 for rendering\n4. Load or retrieve CEL frame data for frame index 1 (non-async)\n5. Validate CEL file pointer is non-null (assert if null)\n6. Get CEL file properties: table index, height, mode value, DWORD field\n7. Calculate texture dimensions from gathered CEL properties\n8. Load and draw the CEL texture to graphics buffer\n9. If texture load succeeds, render frame vertices at adjusted Y position\n\nParameters:\n  pnCelFile (ECX) - Pointer to CEL file handle/context structure\n  nYPosition (EDX) - Y coordinate for frame rendering (adjusted by -1 internally)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; renders directly to graphics context\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts and calls ReportError(-1) if CEL file pointer is NULL (line 0xCE)\n  - Early exit if LoadOrRetrieveCelFrameData returns 0 (frame not available)\n  - Early exit if LoadAndDrawCelTexture returns 0 (texture load failed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  4 - Alpha blend mode constant\n  0x40 - Constant color value for rendering\n  3 - Frame render mode passed to LoadAndDrawCelTexture\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Draw all pixels (no color key)\n  1 - Frame index for LoadOrRetrieveCelFrameData",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1ee298678c0ac12cdaa2193e5b3d95595ff43bcab12dae65c98a765cb4bfa7d2",
