      "name": "PlayBinkVideo",
      "signature": "undefined PlayBinkVideo(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Opens and plays a Bink video file with specified mode, handling graphics/sound setup and message processing during playback.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Check if video already playing (DAT_6f884df0) - exit if yes\n    2. Initialize Bink sound system\n    3. Determine search scope based on expansion flag (0x4 or 0x5)\n    4. Open video file with SFileOpenFileEx\n    5. Open Bink file with mode flags (0x800000 base, OR'd with mode bits)\n    6. Calculate buffer dimensions from dimensions table\n    7. Get initial timestamp (500ms offset for timeout)\n    8. Loop: Process messages, handle Bink frames, lock/copy to backbuffer\n    9. On completion or user exit, close handles and restore sound volume\n\n  Parameters:\n    pszFilePath (ECX): Pointer to video filename to load\n    nVideoMode (EDX): Video mode flags (1=alt1, 2=alt2, 3=alt3, else default)\n\n  Returns:\n    void - Sets DAT_6f884df0 to handle on success, NULL on error\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Exits early if DAT_6f884df0 already set (prevents double-open)\n    - Sets DAT_6f884dfc flag (0=playing, 1=finished)\n    - Monitors DAT_6f885454 for abort signal\n    - User can close window via WM_CLOSE or alt-tab",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
