      "name": "InitializeGlideWindowInternal",
      "signature": "undefined4 InitializeGlideWindowInternal(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the Glide 3D graphics subsystem window and texture memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert that Glide window is not already open (g_bGlideWindowOpen == 0)\n2. Initialize character bitmap resources via InitializeCharacterBitmap\n3. Configure screen dimensions based on nScreenMode:\n   - Mode 0: 640x480 with color format 7\n   - Mode 1+: 800x600 with color format 8\n4. Open Glide window via grSstWinOpen with configured resolution\n5. If window open succeeds:\n   a. Query GPU capabilities if g_bQueryGpuCapabilities set\n   b. Get TMU count, texture alignment, UMA support via grGet\n   c. Configure vertex layout, filter modes, depth/color masks\n   d. Configure texture combine states for each TMU\n   e. Set chromakey value to 0xFF (magenta transparency)\n6. Calculate texture memory layout:\n   a. Query min/max texture addresses for each TMU\n   b. Compute total available texture memory\n   c. Validate minimum memory requirement (>= 4MB check)\n   d. Partition memory between TMU0/TMU1 texture pools\n   e. Initialize texture cache and range tables\n7. Initialize remaining Glide resources and set game mode ordinal\n\nParameters:\n  dwBinkRender (ECX) - HWND handle for Bink video rendering context, stored to g_dwBinkRender\n  nScreenMode (EDX) - Screen mode selector: 0 = 640x480, non-zero = 800x600\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 on success, 0 on failure (grSstWinOpen failed or insufficient texture memory)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If grSstWinOpen returns 0, logs error and returns failure\n  - If total texture memory < 4MB, logs warning and returns early\n  - Mode 0/2 enable fullscreen (g_dwLastError = 1), mode 1 uses windowed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x280 = 640 (low-res width)\n  0x1e0 = 480 (low-res height)\n  0x320 = 800 (high-res width)\n  0x258 = 600 (high-res height)\n  0x8e = Line 142 for FogAssert\n  0x1ccccc = 1,883,980 minimum TMU1 allocation\n  0x300000 = 3,145,728 max single TMU cache size\n  0x100000 = 1,048,576 max TMU texture pool size\n\nError Handling:\n  - FogAssert triggered if g_bGlideWindowOpen already set\n  - ReportError(-1) called after failed assertion\n  - Insufficient memory logged via QueueLogMessage",
