      "name": "WorldToScreen",
      "signature": "undefined WorldToScreen(int param_1, int param_2, int param_3, int * param_4, int * param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts 3D world coordinates to 2D isometric screen coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Compute adjusted X coordinate relative to texture reference point\n     (nWorldX - g_dwGlideTextureData) * 0x18 >> 0x10\n  2. Compute adjusted Y coordinate relative to texture reference point\n     (nWorldY - g_dwGlideTextureSize) * 0x18 >> 0x10\n  3. Calculate relative distance as sum of adjusted coordinates\n  4. Look up depth scaling factor from texture cache indexed by Z coordinate\n  5. Apply isometric projection matrix to compute screen X coordinate\n     centered on screen center with half-width offset\n  6. Apply isometric projection matrix to compute screen Y coordinate\n     centered on screen center with -0x20 (32-pixel) offset\n\nParameters:\n  nWorldX - World X coordinate (passed in ECX via __fastcall)\n  nWorldY - World Y coordinate (passed in EDX via __fastcall)\n  nWorldZ - World Z/depth coordinate (passed in EAX via __fastcall)\n  pOutScreenX - Pointer to output screen X coordinate (stack param 0x10)\n  pOutScreenY - Pointer to output screen Y coordinate (stack param 0x14)\n\nReturns:\n  Void - Output written to *pOutScreenX and *pOutScreenY\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Uses hardcoded magic values (0x99800, 0x9c9b8, 0x2d4, 0x109a08, 0x5a800)\n  indicating isometric projection constants. Bitmask 0x1fff suggests 8192-byte\n  alignment for texture cache entries. Screen coordinates centered at\n  (g_dwScreenWidth/2, g_dwScreenHeight/2) with Y offset of -0x20 pixels.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d41c7ec353459460daaaf538d82aae8bd09b8251ac9eab10c6060d771cf8c9dd",
