      "name": "CloseSmackerHandle",
      "signature": "undefined CloseSmackerHandle(int * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Closes a Smacker video handle and clears the context structure.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Check if status byte at offset +0x4 is 's' (0x73, indicating open/active state)\n  2. If open AND handle at offset 0x0 is non-NULL, call _SmackClose to close the handle\n  3. Zero the handle pointer at offset 0x0\n  4. Zero the status byte at offset +0x4 to mark as closed\n\n  Parameters:\n    pSmackerCtx (ECX) - Pointer to Smacker context structure\n      [0x0] DWORD - Smacker handle (NULL if not allocated)\n      [0x4] BYTE  - Status flag ('s' = active/open, 0 = closed/inactive)\n\n  Returns:\n    void - No return value. Modifies context structure in-place.\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Safely handles NULL handle (skips _SmackClose call)\n    - Handles already-closed context (if status != 's', only clears status byte)\n    - Guarantees idempotent operation (safe to call multiple times)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:63bcbb1f7df6b1748b4dd095c8d5bd046a23cb88d2f00ab06558a9c49dfdb944",
