      "name": "ConvertPalettedSpriteToRgb565",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertPalettedSpriteToRgb565(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Convert paletted sprite data from Smack video to RGB565 format for GPU upload.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load source/destination buffer pointers from globals\n  2. Process 0x40 (64) rows of sprite data\n  3. For each row, process 0x100 (256) pixels in pairs:\n     a. Read palette index from source buffer (g_pSpriteBuffer2)\n     b. Look up RGB888 value in palette at pPalette[index*3]\n     c. Convert RGB888 to RGB565:\n        - Red:   (R & 0xF8) << 8  (5 bits, positions 11-15)\n        - Green: (G & 0xFC) << 3  (6 bits, positions 5-10)\n        - Blue:  (B >> 3)         (5 bits, positions 0-4)\n     d. Write RGB565 pixel to output buffers (g_pSpriteBuffer0, g_pSpriteBuffer1)\n  4. Advance all buffer pointers by 0x200 (512 bytes = 256 pixels * 2 bytes/pixel)\n\nParameters:\n  pPalette (ECX) - pointer to 256-entry RGB888 palette (768 bytes total)\n                   from Smack video structure at offset 0x6C\n\nReturns:\n  void - output written to g_pSpriteBuffer0 and g_pSpriteBuffer1\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Processes exactly 64x256 = 16384 pixels (128x128 texture split across 2 mipmaps)\n  - Dual output buffers support split mipmap rendering for Glide GPU\n  - Source buffer offset -0x100 reads from previous row for interlaced access",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c98dd3143dcbf6ead3ed64b14326232e52a156a370886d0de99ca226696683eb",
