      "name": "RenderTileRow",
      "signature": "void RenderTileRow(TileProject * pTileProj, int nStartX, int nStartY, int nClipX, int nClipY)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Renders a row of tiles to the screen with color blending and clipping\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate tile indices are within bounds (0-9)\n  2. Iterate through tiles in the row (from nStartY index)\n  3. For each tile, fetch tile data from TileProject structure\n  4. Perform bounds checking against clip rectangle\n  5. Decode tile components and calculate screen coordinates\n  6. Blend colors between adjacent tiles using fixed-point math\n  7. Call WorldToScreen to transform world coordinates to screen space\n  8. Draw vertex arrays with combined/interpolated color values\n\nParameters:\n  pTileProj (ECX)  - Pointer to TileProject structure containing tile data\n  nStartX (EDX)    - Starting tile X coordinate (0x0D bit shift applied)\n  nStartY (Stack)  - Starting tile Y coordinate\n  nClipX (Stack)   - Clip rectangle X coordinate\n  nClipY (Stack)   - Clip rectangle Y coordinate\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 0x1 if rendering succeeded, 0x0 if clip bounds violated or tile bounds invalid\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset|Size|Field       |Type   |Description\n  0x0   |4   |dwField0    |DWORD  |Unknown field\n  0x50  |4   |nTileCount  |DWORD  |Number of tiles in row\n  0x54  |4   |pTileData   |void*  |Pointer to tile data array\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Invalid tile index (out of 0-9 range): Calls FogAssert and returns\n  - No tiles in row (nTileCount == 0): Skips to cleanup\n  - Tiles outside clip bounds: Performs boundary checks with floating-point comparisons",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
