      "name": "InitializeGlideGraphics",
      "signature": "int InitializeGlideGraphics(int nX, int nY)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initialize Glide 3D graphics subsystem with hardware detection\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if already initialized (DAT_6f88543c != 0)\n  2. If initialized, deinitialize first via FUN_6f878859(0xffffffff)\n  3. Store X/Y parameters (dwX, dwY) to globals\n  4. Log \"Initializing for Glide...\" message\n  5. Allocate tile texture buffers\n  6. Initialize multiple graphics subsystems\n  7. Call grGlideInit() for Glide 3D hardware init\n  8. Set initialization flag to 1\n  9. Query and log hardware info (device, vendor, renderer, version)\n  10. Initialize texture management, fog, blend modes, and gamma tables\n  11. Allocate and initialize critical section mutex for thread safety\n  12. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  dwX (ECX):  Screen width or X coordinate (fastcall param 1)\n  dwY (EDX):  Screen height or Y coordinate (fastcall param 2)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If DAT_6f88543c is already set, performs reinitialization\n  Allocates critical section via FogMemAlloc (18 bytes)\n  Updates global g_pCriticalSection for thread synchronization\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset|Size|Field|Type|Description\n  -------|-----|-----|-----------|---------------\n  0x0|4|dwX|int|Screen width parameter (fastcall ECX)\n  0x4|4|dwY|int|Screen height parameter (fastcall EDX)",
