      "name": "InitializeGraphicsRendering",
      "signature": "int InitializeGraphicsRendering(int nClearBuffer, dword dwColorHigh, dword dwColorLow)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initialize graphics rendering engine and prepare for frame buffer operations\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if game abort flag is set (g_dwGameAbort) - return 0 if aborting\n  2. Set rendering initialization flag (DAT_6f88545c) to 1\n  3. Acquire critical section pointer, lazily initialize if needed\n  4. Enter critical section for thread-safe access to graphics state\n  5. Clear graphics buffers if bClearBuffer parameter is non-zero\n  6. Zero out three color/state buffer locations (DAT_6f885448, 0x44c, 0x450)\n  7. Enable chromakey mode (transparent color key support) via grChromakeyMode(1)\n  8. Set active drawing color to white (0xFF, 0xFF, 0xFF) via FUN_6f8774d0\n  9. Return success code 1\n\nParameters:\n  bClearBuffer - If non-zero, clear graphics buffer (ECX register, __fastcall)\n  dwColorHigh - Upper byte of 24-bit color value (EDX register, __fastcall)\n  dwColorLow - Lower byte of 24-bit color value (stack parameter)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Success, graphics engine initialized and ready for rendering\n  0 - Game abort in progress, initialization skipped\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function returns immediately with 0 if game shutdown is in progress\n  - Critical section initialized lazily on first call via FUN_6f878859\n  - Bit-shifting color components into 32-bit buffer clear value\n  - Function uses __fastcall convention (ECX/EDX first two params)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:ac64ec35edda9cc32b6688470eca3c3c1ec822213a3e5f12a014dc0d05722dad",
