      "name": "GetScreenClipBounds",
      "signature": "void GetScreenClipBounds(int nPanelType, int nScrollMode, tagRECT * prClip, int * pnXScrollOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Computes the screen clipping rectangle for tile rendering based on panel type and scroll mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate prClip pointer is non-NULL (assert and fatal error if NULL)\n2. Initialize clip rect to full screen bounds: left=0, right=g_dwScreenWidth, top=0\n3. Set bottom to g_dwScreenHeight - 0x2F (47 pixels reserved for UI bar)\n4. Branch based on nScrollMode:\n   - If nScrollMode == 0 (static panel mode):\n     a. Set left padding to -0x20 (-32), extend bottom to height - 0x0F\n     b. If nPanelType == 1 (left panel): shrink right to screenWidth/2\n     c. If nPanelType == 2 (right panel): set left to screenWidth/2 - 0x20\n   - If nScrollMode != 0 (scroll/isometric mode):\n     a. Validate pnXScrollOffset is non-NULL (assert and fatal error if NULL)\n     b. Calculate quarter-width: (screenWidth + rounding) / 4\n     c. If nPanelType == 1: scroll offset = -quarterWidth, shrink bounds by quarterWidth\n     d. If nPanelType == 2: scroll offset = +quarterWidth, shrink bounds by quarterWidth\n\nParameters:\n  nPanelType (ECX) - Panel identifier: 0=none, 1=left panel (inventory/skills), 2=right panel (stats/quests)\n  nScrollMode (EDX) - Scroll mode: 0=static panel, non-zero=isometric scroll view\n  prClip (Stack+0x4) - Pointer to tagRECT receiving computed clip bounds (must be non-NULL)\n  pnXScrollOffset (Stack+0x8) - Pointer to int receiving X scroll offset (required when nScrollMode != 0)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results stored in prClip and optionally pnXScrollOffset\n  Asserts and calls ReportError(-1) if prClip is NULL\n  Asserts and calls ReportError(-1) if pnXScrollOffset is NULL when nScrollMode != 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2F (47) - Bottom UI bar height offset\n  0x20 (32) - Left padding for static panels\n  0x0F (15) - Extended bottom offset for static panels",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
