      "name": "ProcessTileProjectRendering",
      "signature": "int ProcessTileProjectRendering(TileProject * pTileProj, int nStartX, int nStartY, char bAlphaBlendMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Renders tile project geometry to screen with color blending and palette decoding.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Allocate graphics buffer for tile project vertex data\n    2. Configure graphics state: color combine, alpha blend mode, texture filtering\n    3. If graphics background color is set, delegate to FUN_6f877f80 for special handling\n    4. Initialize tile component parameters\n    5. For each tile component in project:\n       - Decode tile position (X, Y coordinates from component data)\n       - Check if tile is within viewport bounds (0x20 = 32 pixel offset)\n       - If in bounds, extract palette indices from palette table\n       - Render quad vertices with decoded palette colors\n       - Draw quad (4 vertices, 0x1c=28 bytes per vertex)\n\n  Parameters:\n    pTileProj: Pointer to TileProject structure (272 bytes), contains tile component array\n    nStartX: Viewport minimum X coordinate for clipping\n    nStartY: Viewport minimum Y coordinate for clipping\n    bAlphaBlendMode: Alpha blend mode (-1=opaque mode, 4=transparent with color value)\n\n  Returns:\n    1 if any tiles were rendered successfully\n    0 if buffer allocation failed or no tiles within viewport bounds\n\n  Special Cases:\n    Skips rendering if GetGraphicsBackgroundColor() returns non-zero\n    Tile coordinates right-shifted 5 bits (>>5) for palette lookup\n    Viewport bounds include 0x20 (32) pixel margins for quad vertex expansion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:860bf889655485da891b8221f5a80148a4c2ce7560cc1e072d7fa29379837f38",
