      "name": "RenderTileProjected",
      "signature": "undefined4 RenderTileProjected(TileProject * pTileProj, int nY, int nPanelId)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Renders isometric tile projection within a clipped panel region.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Allocate buffer for tile projection (calls AllocateTileProjectBuffer)\n  2. Return 0x0 if allocation fails\n  3. Initialize graphics state: color combine, alpha blend, texture filter\n  4. Get background color; return if non-zero (renders from fallback path)\n  5. Get panel clip rect using nPanelId\n  6. Iterate through all tile components in pTileProj->unknown_50\n  7. For each component:\n     a. Calculate screen position (pTileComp X + nY offset)\n     b. Test if component overlaps clip rectangle bounds\n     c. If visible: decode palette indices, render 4-vertex quad via grDrawVertexArrayContiguous\n  8. Return render success flag (1 = rendered, 0 = no render)\n\nParameters:\n  pTileProj (ECX):  TileProject structure containing tile components and metadata\n  nY (EDX):         Y-offset to apply to all tile positions\n  nPanelId (Stack): Panel identifier for determining clip rectangle bounds\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 0x0 if allocation fails, 0x0 or 0x1 if background renders, 1 if tiles rendered\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Non-zero background color triggers alternate render path (RenderTileRow)\n  - Tile components outside clip rect are culled (not rendered)\n  - Palette indices use 0x20 bit alignment (>>5 shift)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:3e3eaf32ec0058ee5ebb88d3774d96f7e687930f0bd6bbb110610eba1d338e2a",
