      "name": "InitializeCodePageLocale",
      "signature": "int InitializeCodePageLocale(int nCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes code page locale settings and character classification tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section 0x19 for thread safety\n2. Resolve code page identifier from input parameter\n3. Check if code page matches cached value - return 0 if already initialized\n4. Return -1 if code page is 0 (invalid)\n5. Search predefined code page table (0x6f8845a0) for matching entry\n6. If found in table: use predefined lead byte ranges from table\n7. If not found: call GetCPInfo() to get code page info from Windows\n8. Clear character class table (256 bytes at 0x6f887620)\n9. For MBCS code pages: mark lead byte ranges with appropriate flags\n10. Initialize locale data buffers and character tables\n11. Cache the new code page value\n12. Release critical section and return status\n\nParameters:\n  nCodePage (int) - Windows code page identifier (e.g., 932 for Japanese, 1252 for Western)\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success (code page initialized or already cached)\n  -1 - Failure (invalid code page or GetCPInfo failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Code page 0 triggers fallback initialization via InitializeLocaleDataBuffers\n  - Predefined table supports up to 5 entries (0x30 bytes each)\n  - MBCS code pages have MaxCharSize > 1 and use lead byte ranges\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x19  - Critical section index for locale operations\n  0x30  - Size of each code page table entry (48 bytes)\n  0x40  - Character class table size in DWORDs (256 bytes total)\n  0x04  - Lead byte flag in character class table\n  0x08  - Non-lead-byte MBCS flag\n\nStructure Layout (g_aCodePageTable entry at 0x6f8845a0):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x00    4     dwCodePage      Code page identifier\n  0x04    4     dwMaxCharSize   Maximum character size\n  0x10    16    aLeadByteRanges Lead byte range pairs (up to 5 pairs + null terminator)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1002f87fdc99e199d60f8fed95eee9ff2ea93ce811eaaa9cd38db7ba9dccaafb",
