      "name": "RenderCelGraphic",
      "signature": "undefined4 RenderCelGraphic(int * param_1, int param_2, int param_3, uint param_4, int param_5, int param_6, uint param_7)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Renders a CEL graphic with transformation and alpha blending to screen coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load or retrieve CEL frame data from pCelData pointer (0x0=success)\n  2. Extract CEL file metadata: table index, height, blend mode, pixel offset\n  3. Perform coordinate transformations via FUN_6f8755a0:\n     - Compute scaled texture coordinates (fTexU1, fTexU2, fTexV1, fTexV2)\n     - Scale by source CEL pixel dimensions (stored at DAT_6f881b3c, DAT_6f881b40)\n  4. Calculate quad vertices by converting world coordinates to screen space:\n     - Each WorldToScreen call adds vertex to g_VertexArray (offset 0x6f886ed0)\n     - Quad represents 2D CEL bounding box with 4 corners\n  5. Apply direction offset if nDirection matches param5 (1=left, 2=right):\n     - Offset amount = g_dwScreenWidth >> 2 (divide by 4)\n  6. Perform screen-space bounds checking (clipping):\n     - If any corner outside visible area [0, g_dwScreenWidth) x [0, g_dwScreenHeight-47]\n     - Return 1 (out of bounds, skip rendering)\n  7. Setup graphics rendering state via FUN_6f875720\n  8. Configure blend mode based on nBlendMode parameter:\n     - 3: SetAlphaBlendMode(2)\n     - 4: SetAlphaBlendMode(3)\n     - 5,7: SetAlphaBlendMode(1) with alpha channel\n     - 0,1,2,6: SetAlphaBlendMode(4) with dither, const color (0x40/0x80/0xc0)\n  9. Set texture filtering and color combining modes\n  10. Render textured quad via grDrawVertexArrayContiguous (5 vertices, 0x1c stride)\n\nParameters:\n  pCelData [ECX]  - Pointer to CEL file data structure (CelFileInfo*)\n  nX [EDX]        - Base X coordinate in world units\n  nWidth [R8D]    - Viewport width or scaling factor\n  nBlendMode [R9D] - Blend/transparency mode (0=normal, 3,4=alpha, 5,7=additive)\n  nDirection [Stack] - Direction offset (1=left, 2=right, else=center)\n  param6 [Stack]  - Additional parameter for FUN_6f875720\n\nReturns:\n  0x0 - CEL frame load failed, rendering skipped\n  0x1 - CEL rendered successfully\n  0x1 - Clipping check failed (bounds outside viewport)",
