      "name": "DecimalStringToDouble",
      "signature": "void DecimalStringToDouble(_CRT_DOUBLE * pOutputDouble, byte * pDecimalString)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Convert a decimal string to a double-precision floating-point number.\n\nThis function parses a decimal ASCII string representation into a double-precision\nfloating-point value using the CRT library's decimal parsing functions. It includes\nstack canary validation for security purposes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize stack canary check using XOR of global canary and stack pointer\n2. Parse the input decimal string into a long double (12-byte) structure\n3. Convert the parsed long double value to a 64-bit double precision format\n4. Verify stack canary integrity before returning\n5. Call stack checking function for security validation\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputDouble: Pointer to _CRT_DOUBLE output buffer for the converted value\n- pDecimalString: Pointer to null-terminated decimal ASCII string to parse\n\nReturns:\n- void (output written to pOutputDouble)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses stack canary verification (XOR-based guard against buffer overflows)\n- Handles conversion from extended precision (long double) to standard precision (double)\n- Input validation performed by ParseDecimalNumber function\n\nStack Canary Security:\nThe function uses a global canary value (DAT_6fc406bc) XORed with the stack\npointer to detect stack corruption. The canary is checked before returning.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.12a",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:4a4fbdf0c4344cbfc3ffd62988f04f852538b7a2897b4bef996c9ea28c819b40",
